{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071759-ghost-shield-interpretations","id":1071759,"title":"Ghost Shield Interpretations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-01T11:18:06-07:00","id":1071759,"title":"Ghost Shield Interpretations","content":"Help my group settle some disagreements on how this spell works.<br /> <br /> We all take it as a given that the protection against deathly supernatural powers extends to vampiric disciplines and whatever sin-eaters call their powers.<br /> <br /> But with the extra reach, does it provide protection:<br /> -against a stone thrown with ghostly telekinesis or a punch from someone possessed by a ghost? I say it only protects against materialized ghosts - what is the consensus?<br /> -against a vampire or sin-eater punching you in the gut (I think it only applies to ghosts, some us think it clearly should apply to vampires, and a couple insist sin-eaters too)?<br /> <br /> Finally, how does the protection against physical attack work? I assumed it was still a clash of wills, but several of my fellows state that protection against direct physical attacks never work that way, and it should manifest as armor dots.<br /> <br /> I know we can tweak the rules however we want, but I'd like to know if there are official rules here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T11:43:18-07:00","id":1071767,"title":"","content":"Ghost Shield protects you from direct ghostly powers and, with Reach, their physical attacks. It doesn't protect you from physical objects. A chair hurled at you from across the room is still going to hurt when it hits you. A possessed person's fist flying at you is still a fist. A fire started by a ghost is still a fire and your Ghost Shield won't save you from the choking smoke or a burning beam falling on your head.<br /> <br /> (You could say the possessed person one is covered under physical attacks. No real reason to go either way save what works best for your games.)<br /> <br /> Ghost Shield won't save you from a Geist swinging for you. Geists aren't undead. From a Vamp... See above.<br /> <br /> And, finally, yeah, it's always a Clash.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}